            <ArticleTitle>Predictors of patients' experience of pain in EMG.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>629-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The important features that predict the amount of pain experienced by patients with low back pain who undergo needle electromyography were the patients' assessment of their own pain, their trait-anxiety levels, and female sex. Although it does not influence EMG pain, information about the test will decrease the anxiety of patients coming for testing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
